WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.400
The AV-98,
aka the Ingram patrol labor.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.520
6.02 tons.
8.02 meters high.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.700
SCB powered.
SCLM drive system.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.990
Armed and ready for combat with a
37 millimeter revolver and stun baton.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.540
Designed specifically
for police use...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.200
to make a psychological impact
on the community...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.540
to deter criminals
while making the public feel safe.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.280
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.070
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.080
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.450
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.300
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.510
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.270
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.440
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.280
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.790
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.460
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:02.180
Reunion

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:22.160
Upper right arm actuators 1 and 2...

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:23.530
completely shot.

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:27.540
Lumbar vertebrae rotators...

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:29.000
also destroyed.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:32.170
The entire hip section
needs to be replaced.

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:34.960
It'll have to go back to the factory.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:39.180
Yeah, there's not much
choice when it's this bad.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:44.220
Make a full checklist.
We'll send it out first thing tomorrow.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:47.430
Start the electrical system diagnostic.

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:48.270
Roger.

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:51.150
Oh well...

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:56.190
Ever since Division 2 was formed,
I've pulled a lot of overtime.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:59.780
My deepest apologies.

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:04.740
That was quite a pounding.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:07.870
That's the least of it.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:12.210
We can fix machine 2. I'm more
worried about the human damage.

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:14.920
They're both in the hospital?

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:23.510
And a shooting!
How did it come to this?

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:27.010
We won't know until
Kumagami wakes up.

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:29.020
Can you believe it, Mr. Sakaki?

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:34.230
The Labor that wrecked machine 2
actually took off and flew.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:41.900
Astonishing. Labors were
created for construction work.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:45.320
A flying Labor is completely pointless.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:46.950
Completely.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:52.330
...but it <i>wasn't</i> a plane,
so it was using sheer brute thrust.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:56.090
It couldn't have had much fuel.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:58.300
Flying probably used ALL its fuel!

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:01.010
I'll bet it can't move at all right now.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:08.010
Exactly! It may have escaped,
but it couldn't have gone far!

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:11.270
Don't you agree, Ms. Izumi?

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.230
Oh, I wouldn't know.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:20.440
From the middle of Tokyo Bay,
to the middle of Chiba Prefecture.

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:25.200
You've pinpointed their secret base?

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:28.950
I don't know about a secret base...

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:33.870
That's a huge area!
What good is that?

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:38.840
It looks like you miss Shinohara, Ota.

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:40.670
What do you mean?

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.880
Our fighting strength
is already down 50%.

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:48.850
With all due respect,
Sir, that's not true!

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:53.100
I'll work as hard as Shinohara
and Kumagami combined!

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:59.060
Unfortunately, Ota, your machine
was sent back to the factory.

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:00.650
It'll be gone for quite a while.

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:06.360
Excuse me, Captain.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:11.040
Captain Nagumo's at the hospital.
I'm waiting for her call.

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:18.420
Izumi, I know you're worried
about your partner...

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:21.550
but you still have work to do.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.760
Yes, Sir!

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:28.140
So get moving!
We need some tea out here.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:33.680
And let it steep a while.
I like it strong.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:36.940
Izumi's having a tough time.

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:39.940
She'll have to handle both
Ota's job and her own.

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:49.950
You'll make it, Hiromi?

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:54.200
Miss Izumi, over here.

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:00.500
What's up with Kana?

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:02.750
They'll show it again.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:07.170
Breaking news

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:11.220
A strange flying object crashed
in the mountains of Chiba.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:16.230
It may be connected to the
Labor dogfight at Tokyo's Haruumi.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:34.990
Finish the breakdown,
then begin loading.

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:37.410
Should we leave the wings?

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:40.250
They've been expended.
Just leave them.

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:45.420
Here, Bud.

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:52.050
A fake covering!

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:53.600
Call it a disguise.

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:58.430
Everyone, drive as safely as possible.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:06.900
Keep to the speed limit.
Jaritra, monitor the police wavelengths.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.420
Pull over!

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:26.960
All trucks, stop.

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:34.640
Don't leave the cab.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:39.890
We don't got no problem
with our rig, do we?

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:44.310
Are you from the
construction site south of here?

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:45.520
Yep.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:50.740
We had a report of a plane crash.
Have you seen anything?

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:57.780
Shucks! Whole sky lit up
like the day o' reckoning!

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:00.790
I thought we was dead men!

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:02.410
What direction?

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:10.010
I figure 'bout three kilometers thataway.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:12.880
Don't know nothing else 'bout it.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:15.390
Hold it!

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:19.010
Your side mirror is crooked.

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:23.980
Dang, must've brushed
that tree a mite close.

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:29.650
Can I go now?

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:30.940
Yes. Drive safely.

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:44.500
The crash went pretty well,
and it looks like we fooled them.

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:47.040
I guess it's smooth sailing from here on.

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:48.920
Chief Utsumi covers every contingency.

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:50.840
He's also a master showman.

00:08:57.050 --> 00:09:03.310
We just heard from Chiba.
They've retrieved the Griffin.

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:07.770
Excellent! Then we can
prepare for another try.

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:09.610
You're going to try again?

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:11.230
Of course!

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:14.990
I have to take care of
that irritating machine 1!

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:17.660
This is our chance, Kurosaki!

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:40.600
I can't sleep.

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:46.440
Oh? That's wonderful.

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:50.270
Us? We're getting by.

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:55.070
I'm sorry about our casualties,
but there is one silver lining.

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:56.150
What's that?

00:09:56.900 --> 00:10:01.660
We've proved that the economy
Ingram isn't up to Patlabor duty.

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:09.000
That's true. Well, you've
had a long day. Get some rest.

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:15.380
Izumi, are you still up?

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:18.510
I couldn't sleep.

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:22.260
Did the Labor from
Haruumi crash in Chiba?

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:23.970
We don't know yet.

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:27.180
I can't relax until I know for sure.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:30.060
I do have some news that may help.

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:35.150
Kumagami's operation was a success.
Her progress is good.

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:37.070
Thank goodness.

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:42.120
And there's no reason for
Shinohara to stay at the hospital.

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:45.120
Now get some sleep.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:48.330
After all, we don't know when
you'll be called back to duty.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:11:00.470
Miss Izumi! The news!
The news! Get up, hurry!

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:04.430
There's a story on TV! Hurry!

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:08.060
...reported seeing a brilliant flash of light.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:14.190
The area is covered with
machine fragments and spilled fuel.

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:21.240
Even through the thick rain,
you can smell the burning oil.

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:24.950
Experts are comparing the wings to...

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:27.450
That's it! I'm positive!

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:28.910
Right? Right?

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:33.130
It's a fiery grave.

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:38.380
Damn! I was looking
forward to a rematch!

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:41.340
It must have self-destructed.

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:46.140
It is now 6:40. Next, the weather.

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:52.060
Something's not right.

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:19.170
Mr. Shinohara,
this isn't a police infirmary.

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.420
When you dress like that,
the other patients get worried.

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:23.840
I'm sorry.

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:29.890
Which way to Officer
Kumagami's room?

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:36.230
He's about 175 cm tall, bangs,
parts his hair on the right.

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:41.690
Squarish chin, glasses, and he
looks like he's always laughing.

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:43.820
That's quite a skill.

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:45.280
What?

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:47.740
His talent for portraits.

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:49.790
Hey, give that back!

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:51.540
Yeah, that's him.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:57.880
How are you feeling, Lt. Kumagami?

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:01.380
Hey, you don't look so bad.

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:02.800
What do you mean, "so bad"?

00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:05.880
I'm going back,
so I came to say goodbye.

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:07.140
Are you all right?

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:10.890
Don't worry about me,
take care of yourself.

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:13.850
Aren't they moving you
to the police infirmary today?

00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:17.440
Yes, but I'd rather stay here...
it's closer to the station.

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:21.270
Everyone at work is pulling for you,
so hurry up and get well.

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:22.650
Thank you.

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:26.240
May we continue, now?

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:27.070
Yeah.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:31.160
What's wrong?

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:32.240
Who's this?

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:39.330
Richard Wong. He was in the car
when Lt. Kumagami was shot.

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:44.800
Really? I thought it was Utsumi.
It looks just like him.

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:48.590
Who's that?

00:13:49.590 --> 00:13:51.850
We'd better talk to you
before you head home.

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:06.320
Utsumi? We employ three
men of that name.

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:10.070
He looks like this.

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:14.120
Section Chief Utsumi,
in Planning Division 7?

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:15.910
One moment, please.

00:14:17.710 --> 00:14:20.460
What interest do the police
have in our humble business?

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:23.920
It's just a routine check.

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:28.590
Mr. Utsumi is in
Tsuchiura this week.

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:32.140
What kind of check?

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:38.850
Someone resembling Mr. Utsumi
was spotted at a crime scene.

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:43.060
That's preposterous. When?

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:44.070
Yesterday.

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:48.450
I'm afraid our Utsumi has
been Tsuchiura all this time.

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:51.660
Sorry. Must be a
case of mistaken identity.

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:53.030
Yes, absolutely.

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:57.120
Could we have a picture of
Mr. Utsumi for our records?

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:11.260
Chief Utsumi, it's the main office.

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:12.220
Okay.

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:15.220
Hello, Utsumi speaking.

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:18.560
Oh, Division Manager!

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:23.520
No, I wouldn't worry about it.

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:28.030
Yesterday WAS a failure, but
we're almost ready for another try.

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:32.700
What do you mean,
"project suspended"?

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:37.620
I don't know the details,
but the police know who you are.

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:39.700
Stay away from Tokyo for a while.

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:43.040
Visit South America, or anywhere else.

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:45.500
Wait, Boss...

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:48.210
Asuma!

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:52.340
You're feeling okay?

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:56.640
I'm not too bad -
a couple of cracked ribs.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:58.350
Nothing that needs a hospital.

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:01.180
Don't overexert yourself.
You should go lie down.

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:03.520
Lying down won't help me rest.

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:05.860
How's Kumagami?

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:08.020
She'll be out for a month.

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:12.700
That means a month
of Ota out of control.

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:14.410
Where's Noa?

00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:17.160
Well, she had insomnia...

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:18.490
Insomnia?

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:28.550
She hasn't slept at all?

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:33.170
She couldn't get any sleep.
She was too worried about you.

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:37.640
Come on, you're kidding!

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:40.270
Believe it, lover boy!

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:42.980
Oh, I'm so sorry!

00:16:55.070 --> 00:16:56.740
Wait, time out.

00:16:56.990 --> 00:17:02.200
What's wrong? First you
want practice, and now you want rest.

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:06.040
Izumi doesn't know you're
here yet, does she?

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:09.170
Sometimes she's not too observant.

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:18.140
All right.

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:19.760
You ready?

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:21.510
Please.

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:24.480
Take your best shot.

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:26.850
What are they doing?

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:28.980
Getting motivated.

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:42.700
Hang in there.

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:47.710
What's wrong?

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:51.000
I'm so useless.

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:54.710
Did you suddenly turn useless
in the last few days?

00:17:56.470 --> 00:18:03.310
I was totally useless yesterday.
I couldn't help you or Kumagami...

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:05.230
or Asuma.

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:08.850
I wasn't expecting your help.

00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:12.110
Besides, that whole mess
was Shinohara's fault.

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:13.270
That jerk!

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:15.690
Asuma, remember your ribs!

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:18.780
I couldn't do a thing.

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:22.830
And when I heard the Black Labor
had crashed, I was so relieved!

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:25.040
I'm pathetic.

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:27.620
Step one is recognizing all your flaws.

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:30.670
He could have put that a lot better!

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:34.590
That's the only way
Ota knows how to put it.

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:40.340
Did that help wake you up?

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:43.930
It's time for lunch. Let's go.

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:46.310
Thank you, Ota.

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:49.640
I won't help you beat
yourself up anymore.

00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:52.440
Don't you think they're
a little more motivated now?

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:54.900
And one more thing:

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:58.110
Cry on Shinohara's
shoulder from now on.

00:18:58.490 --> 00:19:00.490
It makes me uncomfortable.

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:04.780
What's the matter with him?

00:19:04.780 --> 00:19:06.790
He's blushing.

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:24.180
I'm afraid he gave us no choice.

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:27.060
So we came this far
only to give up?

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:32.020
Don't look at me like that!
I'm at least as angry as you are!

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:35.230
Sorry, Sir.
You didn't look like it.

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:38.740
Break down the Griffin
and load it onto the carriers.

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:45.660
Chief, Red Rock in Tokyo has
news on the Division Manager.

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:48.240
He's calling in Shaft Security Systems.

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:51.710
Three-S? But that means...

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:54.420
He's covering his bases.

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:58.840
I'll bet he's been in contact with
America, ever since Ogasawara.

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:08.390
Mr. Utsumi, I just heard!
We aren't going to give up, are we?

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:12.890
Company orders. I have no choice.

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:15.610
You sound like a salary man.

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:17.610
I AM a salary man.

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:21.320
I don't like it!
The Griffin's in perfect shape!

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:23.200
It isn't "game over" yet!

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:30.200
That's true. If we still have
the Griffin, it isn't "game over."

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:34.080
Kurosaki, where is Three-S right now?

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:39.380
I told Red Rock and Green River
to keep their eyes open.

00:21:09.990 --> 00:21:13.410
Mr. Sakaki, thanks for
letting us use the hanger.

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:18.210
You didn't have much choice.
The rain soaked the fields.

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:37.060
Hi, I'm back.

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:42.150
Three-S? What's that?

00:21:42.690 --> 00:21:44.400
Shaft Security Systems.

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:46.990
They're a private security agency...

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:51.370
but it would be more accurate
to call them a mercenary army.

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:58.460
They frequently use Labors.
They DO combat Labor crime,

00:21:58.460 --> 00:22:01.090
but it's usually pretty bloody.

00:22:01.290 --> 00:22:02.840
Trying to out-do the military?

00:22:02.840 --> 00:22:06.170
Just the sort of people who'd
start a private war inside a city.

00:22:06.420 --> 00:22:09.640
I've had my eye on them for a while.

00:22:10.600 --> 00:22:14.140
Do you think they're connected
to the Labor show incident?

00:22:14.640 --> 00:22:15.310
Probably.

00:22:15.810 --> 00:22:19.270
I'd like to ride along with
your team for a few days.

00:22:20.060 --> 00:22:21.860
Anytime.

00:22:27.150 --> 00:22:31.240
Lt. Kanuka Clancy, of the
New York Police Department...

00:22:31.240 --> 00:22:33.450
is temporarily assuming
command of Ingram machine 1.

00:22:36.700 --> 00:22:38.120
I hope you're up to it.

00:22:40.670 --> 00:22:41.380
Yes sir!

00:22:45.420 --> 00:22:48.630
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:48.760 --> 00:22:52.350
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:54.680 --> 00:22:58.600
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:06.030 --> 00:23:08.110
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:08.240 --> 00:23:11.030
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:11.110 --> 00:23:15.620
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:18.290 --> 00:23:20.290
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:20.370 --> 00:23:23.130
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:23.380 --> 00:23:27.300
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:30.470 --> 00:23:33.800
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:36.430 --> 00:23:39.060
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:39.020 --> 00:23:41.600
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:41.600 --> 00:23:44.810
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:45.060 --> 00:23:48.900
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
